    en: "<p>Recall from the previous modules:</p><ul><li>Office is <strong>application software</strong> — programs that do the user's work, not system software.</li><li>The <strong>extension</strong> after the dot decides the file type and which program opens it: <span class=\"num\">.docx</span>, <span class=\"num\">.xlsx</span>, <span class=\"num\">.pptx</span>.</li><li>Anything unsaved stays in <strong>memory</strong> and is lost when power goes. Saving moves it to <strong>storage</strong>.</li><li>Cloud computing means your file is kept on a distant server you reach over the internet.</li></ul><p>This module is the theory behind the practical Module 7, so nothing is to be carried out now. The aim is to understand what each tool does and why.</p>"
